   "title": "The Lighthouse Keeper",
   "genre": "fiction",
   "text": "The lighthouse stood white against the grey sea. Mara had kept its lamp for eleven years, and she knew every gull by its cry. That night the storm took the radio, the spare bulb, and \u2014 worst of all \u2014 her certainty. When the small boat appeared between waves, she had only the old oil lamp and her own judgement.",
   "questions": [
    {
     "stem": "What does the lighthouse symbolise?",
     "options": [
      "Safety",
      "Danger",
      "Isolation",
      "Guidance"
     ],
     "answer": 3,
     "explain": "It guides the boat despite the storm."
    },
    {
